API-13: take a wet runoff step while rainfall is forced on a subcatchment

computeRunoffTimestep() uses WET_STEP only when is_raining (a gage reports
rain), snow, ponded runoff or a wet LID is present. Rainfall forced on a
subcatchment with swmm_forcing_subcatch_rainfall() (or snowfall with the
snowfall forcing) replaced the gage value in the runoff solver but did not
set is_raining, so with a dry gage the runoff step was DRY_STEP: one long
step computed with the rate in force at its start. Set is_raining when any
subcatchment has an active rainfall or snowfall forcing with a positive
value.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-13_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..2b590da 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -1925,6 +1925,18 @@ void SWMMEngine::stepRunoff(double dt_routing) noexcept {
             if (ctx_.gages.rainfall[static_cast<std::size_t>(g)] > 0.0)
                 is_raining = true;
         }
+        // Precipitation forced on a subcatchment through the API also
+        // requires a wet runoff step.
+        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < ctx_.forcing.subcatch_rainfall_mode.size(); ++i) {
+            if (ctx_.forcing.subcatch_rainfall_mode[i] != ForcingMode::NONE &&
+                ctx_.forcing.subcatch_rainfall_value[i] > 0.0)
+                is_raining = true;
+        }
+        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < ctx_.forcing.subcatch_snowfall_mode.size(); ++i) {
+            if (ctx_.forcing.subcatch_snowfall_mode[i] != ForcingMode::NONE &&
+                ctx_.forcing.subcatch_snowfall_value[i] > 0.0)
+                is_raining = true;
+        }
 
         // A2. Update climate state
         int doy = datetime::dayOfYear(abs_time);
